turning a profit and protecting the  environment this ice cream parlor pulls  it off the Florida ice brand sells for  one euro 20 a scoop it's tasty and it's  also ethical the most important thing is  that the manufacturing process is carbon  neutral we care about climate protection  and people who go to an ice cream parlor  can relate to that and maybe want to do  something for the environment  Olaf Hearn has been making Florida ice  in a Berlin suburb for over 30 years  his son is head of marketing and has  taken the company's marketing strategy  in a new direction my son gave me a  wake-up call he studied hydrogeology at  university I listened to what he had to  say at that point I hadn't paid any  attention to the environment at all no  it's my hobby the company's invested  over a million euros in clean technology  for things like its vehicle cooling  systems these are for these vehicles all  have a tech tech cooling so the  compressor can be taken out and when  we're out in the city we're using a  silent cooling device that's carbon  neutral we don't yet have electric  motors but we're working on it the  production process is powered by  renewable energy sources such as the  solar power units on the factory roof  demand for the panel's rose in part  thanks to companies like Florida ice  there's also a growing number of solar  parks in Germany if all the solar panels  in the country were pieced together  they'd cover an area larger than Lake  Constance  until a few years ago the panels were  manufactured in Germany but these days  production has been relocated to Asia  all that's left here in Germany are the  industry service providers such as  quality control here at the photovoltaic  Institute in Berlin environmental  engineers test the standards of solar  panels and modules using methods devised  here at the Institute methods such as  the peel test we test the workmanship of  the modules to see if the individual  layers are held together with sufficient  strength to do that we peel off layers  and measure how wide they are that  allows us to calculate how strong they  are if they're well made or if there are  production errors their skills are in  demand  the Institute earns revenues of some two  and a half million euros a year from  quality control of solar panels its  founder is reaping the benefits of his  visionary idealism the whole idea of  doing something with solar energy was  born out of environmental concerns I  took a course in solar energy in 1986  and gained a doctorate in the field in  93 I went into it as an idealist now  it's big business Florida ice is also a  bigger business than it looks these days  it supplies supermarkets and  manufactures some 10 million litres of  ice cream a year the family is proud  that its electricity needs haven't grown  even though the business now makes four  times as much ice cream as it did five  years ago  all of Hern says their investments have  paid off and regrets more companies  aren't following their lead  even though climate change is gathering  pace we need to look out for our  grandchildren  hopefully the worst-case scenario can be  averted I'm not the type to spread alarm  and despondency but I have to say it's  serious do something get active Olaf  Hearn is doing something and if all goes  to plan Florida ice production will be  completely carbon neutral within the  next three years  you
 

